<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Casimir I of Opole</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1178–1230</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Kazimierz I of Opole</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Casimir I of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/opole">Opole</a> (c. 1178–1230) was a Piast duke of Opole and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/raciborz">Racibórz</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/upper-silesia">Upper Silesia</a> from 1211, a son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mieszko-iv-tanglefoot">Mieszko IV Tanglefoot</a>. He encouraged settlement under German law, founding towns and granting them charters, and moved his residence to Opole, where he built a new castle. His sons <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mieszko-ii-the-fat">Mieszko II the Fat</a> and Władysław succeeded him.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/casimir-i-of-opole.jpg" alt="Casimir I of Opole" width="320" height="294" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Anonymous plate · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kazimierz_I_opolski_seal_1226.PNG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
